{"tool_name":"bamquery","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"bamquery","home":"http://bamquery.iric.ca/","license":"MIT","summary":"Proteogenomic tool to explore the immunopeptidome and prioritize actionable tumor antigens.","addition_date":"2024-03-27T15:08:27.658074Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:06:09.588393Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:bamquery","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"g.ehx@uliege.be","name":"Gr\u00e9gory Ehx","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7018-1770","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Differential gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3223"},{"term":"Peptide immunogenicity prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0252"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"BamQuery","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-023-03029-1","metadata":{"abstract":"MHC-I-associated peptides deriving from non-coding genomic regions and mutations can generate tumor-specific antigens, including neoantigens. Quantifying tumor-specific antigens\u2019 RNA expression in malignant and benign tissues is critical for discriminating actionable targets. We present BamQuery, a tool attributing an exhaustive RNA expression to MHC-I-associated peptides of any origin from bulk and single-cell RNA-sequencing data. We show that many cryptic and mutated tumor-specific antigens can derive from multiple discrete genomic regions, abundantly expressed in normal tissues. BamQuery can also be used to predict MHC-I-associated peptides immunogenicity and identify actionable tumor-specific antigens de novo.","authors":[{"name":"Apavaloaei A."},{"name":"Cuevas M.V.R."},{"name":"Durette C."},{"name":"Ehx G."},{"name":"Gendron P."},{"name":"Hardy M.-P."},{"name":"Kina E."},{"name":"Larouche J.-